<DocsLayout title="RedstoneLimiter documentation" description="Understand every RedstoneLimiter setting. Configure Minecraft redstone lag protection with visual explanations, copy-ready YAML examples, and real source-backed defaults.">
<section class="hero">
<div class="eyebrow">THE OFFICIAL CONFIGURATION GUIDE</div>
<div class="hero-split">
  <div><h1>Keep the redstone.<br/><span style="color:#ef795a">Lose the lag.</span></h1><p class="lead">Control how often redstone machines can activate. Learn exactly what each setting changes, without guessing at YAML or accidentally blocking an entire region.</p><div class="btn-row" style="margin:25px 0 8px"><a href="/guide/" class="button button-primary">Get started &nbsp; →</a><a href="/configuration/" class="button button-secondary">Explore configuration ↗</a></div><div class="kicker" style="margin-top:21px">Actual RedstoneLimiter 3.0.1 source · Config v7</div></div>
  <div class="hero-visual" role="img" aria-label="Illustrated redstone activity moving across circuitry with a limiter stopping an excess signal">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 400 260" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><defs><linearGradient id="wire" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="#fba77f"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#b54131"/></linearGradient><filter id="glow"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="4"/></filter></defs>
  <g stroke="#5d3630" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M28 65h80v53h66M28 194h80v-52h66M225 118h55v-52h92M225 142h55v52h92"/></g><g stroke="url(#wire)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lightpath"><path d="M28 65h80v53h66M28 194h80v-52h66M225 118h55v-52h92M225 142h55v52h92"/></g><g fill="#281d1a" stroke="#a95d47" stroke-width="2"><rect x="164" y="93" width="70" height="74" rx="13"/></g><path d="M184 128l13 12 19-25" stroke="#fda57c" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><g fill="#ffc59b" class="pulse-dot"><circle cx="28" cy="65" r="6"/><circle cx="28" cy="194" r="6"/></g><g fill="#ae6e52"><circle cx="372" cy="66" r="5"/><circle cx="372" cy="194" r="5"/></g><g stroke="#633d33" stroke-width="1"><path d="M178 82V55M220 82V55"/></g><text x="200" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d69a82" font-size="13" font-family="monospace">LIMITER</text><text x="39" y="46" fill="#b58372" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">INPUT</text><text x="310" y="47" fill="#b58372" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">CONTROLLED</text></svg>
  <div class="hero-status"><span>● ACTIVITY OBSERVED</span><span>EXCESS SIGNALS BLOCKED</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="stat-line"><div class="stat"><strong>4</strong><span>Independent limit scopes</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>5s</strong><span>Default activity window</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>28</strong><span>Built-in material keys</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>v7</strong><span>Current config schema</span></div></div>
<div class="divider"></div>
<section><div class="eyebrow">START WITH THE BASICS</div><h2>Three ideas. That's most of the config.</h2><div class="grid-3"><article class="card"><span class="card-ico">01</span><h3>How many?</h3><p><code>max-activations</code> is how many activations to allow in the period. If the limit is 5, the sixth attempt is blocked.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="card-ico">02</span><h3>Over how long?</h3><p><code>duration-millis</code> is the time window used for counting. 5000 milliseconds means 5 seconds.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="card-ico">03</span><h3>How long blocked?</h3><p><code>sustain-millis</code> keeps an over-limit scope temporarily blocked. 2000 milliseconds means 2 seconds.</p></article></div><div style="margin-top:20px"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/how-it-works/">Watch the animated explanations →</a></div></section>
<div class="divider"></div>
<section><div class="eyebrow">A REAL EXAMPLE</div><h2>What does this YAML actually do?</h2><p class="lead">This is a small excerpt of the current default config, not a made-up setting.</p><div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start"><Code code={`blocks:\n  enabled: true\n  period:\n    duration-millis: 5000\n    sustain-millis: 2000\n    sliding: true\n  max-activations:\n    DEFAULT: 5\n    PISTON: 3`} /><div class="card"><div class="mini-label">IN PLAIN ENGLISH</div><h3>For each individual piston…</h3><p>Count up to <strong style="color:#fff">3</strong> recorded activations over the most recent <strong style="color:#fff">5 seconds</strong> before preset/TPS scaling. The next attempt is blocked, with a temporary <strong style="color:#fff">2-second</strong> sustain period. Continuing over-limit attempts can extend that block.</p><p style="margin-top:13px">Other scopes may also block it. The effective limit can be higher when the preset or TPS scaling is more permissive.</p></div></div></section>
<div class="divider"></div>
<section><div class="eyebrow">PICK YOUR NEXT STEP</div><h2>Find what you need.</h2><div class="choice-grid"><a class="choice" href="/configuration/"><span class="mini-label">REFERENCE / 01</span><h3>Explain every config key →</h3><p>Definitions, exact defaults, and what changes when you enable or disable something.</p></a><a class="choice" href="/examples/"><span class="mini-label">RECIPES / 02</span><h3>Stop large lag machines →</h3><p>Focused examples you can merge into the config without replacing unrelated settings.</p></a><a class="choice" href="/calculator/"><span class="mini-label">INTERACTIVE / 03</span><h3>Calculate the real limit →</h3><p>See how preset and TPS scaling affect the effective threshold.</p></a><a class="choice" href="/faq/"><span class="mini-label">HELP / 04</span><h3>Why did this get blocked? →</h3><p>Frequently asked questions based on actual administrator confusion.</p></a></div></section>
